research/project/decision_log.md:73:| 2026-10-06 | Record researcher weight-freezing proposal and distinguish frozen effective strengths, frozen evaluation snapshots and a hypothetical evolving-state replacement. | Current forward resets activity; disabled controls already freeze local adaptation. Calculation success does not prove lasting teaching. Clarification requested; no implementation/scope switch. | Claim freezing fixes learning, relabel gain changes as frozen effective weights, or silently substitute an external answer memory. | Researcher proposed direction; persistent-state alternative remains unresolved. | [Proposal and code evidence](../../documentation/design/research-goals/fixed-weight-proposal.md), [journal](../journal/experiments/2026-10-06-learning-experiments.md) |
research/project/decision_log.md:98:## 2026-10-06: Prepared causal positive-puzzle memory replay
research/project/decision_log.md:99:A separate read-only six-intervention probe is prepared at .codebase/scripts/probe-positive-puzzle-memory.mjs (syntax passes). It compares baseline/first-event/PAM-only/PPL-only/final/restored memories across all legal KQK moves, without adaptation or gate changes. Requires terminal complete pilot and passing prefix audit; do not run concurrently with the live graph. This will distinguish first-event stored contributions from later net changes, without biological necessity or transfer claims. See documentation/design/diagnostics/positive-puzzle-memory.md. Current graph comparison remains live with shuffled/disabled conditions unfinished.
research/project/decision_log.md:101:2026-10-06 preparation update: independent probe auditor .codebase/scripts/audit-positive-puzzle-memory.mjs is prepared and syntax checked. It imports no learning/inference/encoder implementation; reconstructs gain masks from pinned source receipts, checks all legal sets and score arithmetic, and requires original baseline/final/restored score equality. Reports target rank/margin without a fitted threshold. Neither probe nor audit has executed; wait for terminal pilot and passing original prefix audit before graph replay.
research/project/decision_log.md:104:The full-graph positive-puzzle comparison is terminal. Useful-choice and repair-above-absent/disabled gates fail; persistence/causal reset and fixed state pass. Informative/punishment-only KQK remains wrong (Qb3), KRK already succeeds. Absent/disabled preserve initial choices; shuffled degrades KRK and both searched outcomes. Receipt/prefix audits pass 80 certificate uses and 32 enabled updates; exact pending-receipt recovery has zero neural presentations. Trace audit passes 9 informative trajectories/8 explanations/2 defense diagnostics. Complete invocation: 109.5078125 MiB RSS, 916.0918095 s elapsed, 432.437 s CPU, 1692 presentations. Report SHA-256 01a7ab038b03474283580e0dd5f8cb821512dbac4f6833eb45192925dbe5445b. This supersedes pilot live/pending statements; the association prerequisite remains passed, but useful puzzle learning and original reasoning remain unproved. Raw evidence: research/reports/positive-puzzle-pipeline-v1-2026-10-06/README.md. The separate read-only memory probe started only after main/prefix terminal completion and passing audits; its results remain pending.
research/project/decision_log.md:108:The researcher requests that FlyChess investigate likely strong opponent moves and its responses during the opponent's turn, then briefly check and reuse matching analysis after the actual move. Recorded in [pondering design](../../documentation/design/evaluation-and-performance/pondering.md): bounded serial search, history/identity-safe cache reuse, cancellation and fallback, frozen neural memory, and separate latency/compute/strength measurements. This is accepted future search/latency scope, not an implemented feature or biological learning result. Preserve the learning-first sequence and current frozen experiments. No runtime changes or experiments in this documentation update.
research/project/decision_log.md:110:## 2026-10-06 completion: positive-puzzle memory contribution probe
research/project/decision_log.md:111:Read-only full-graph probe is terminal; independent auditor passes six saved-memory interventions and 156 legal-candidate records, exact baseline/final/restored reproduction. Isolated one-edge PAM02 change raises Qh7 score by 0.0004179924726 but improves its margin over Qf5 by only 0.0000000107102; all 26 candidate offsets are nearly common (0.0004178909585 to 0.0004180357791), so choice stays Qf5. Complete first-event/PPL-only states worsen the target margin. Final memory exposes failed Qb3. This supports investigating action-specific eligibility/representation without ruling out coverage; no unique biological cause or validated repair is established. Report SHA-256 496e80a914ba49db835ed1c5033a73caf9f0614419b6423b8f30411de755ff74. Resources: 101.0859375 MiB RSS, 109.4277453 s elapsed, 49.719 s CPU, 156 presentations. Raw evidence: research/reports/positive-puzzle-memory-probe-2026-10-06/README.md. This supersedes probe pending statements. Original useful chess learning and unfamiliar reasoning remain unproved.
research/project/decision_log.md:138:The balanced-only variant passes all seven frozen computational gates on six fresh seeds: acquisition/reversal/ranking switch 6/6, and all four absent/shuffled effect comparisons p=0.015625. Independent record and pending-receipt audits pass 480 transitions/384 local updates; replay is exact with zero new evaluations. Report SHA-256 599af4ca2cb3087fac4a2a0608e10aa2dafe4ed3d5202bdaa909ced969fb01da; 107.6484375 MiB peak RSS, 497.6856848 s elapsed, 283.938 s CPU, 840 evaluations. Raw evidence: research/reports/compartment-input-balanced-2026-10-06/README.md. This is an engineered two-cue association result only, not biological validation, chess reasoning or transfer. It is not a statistical comparison against the other variants. The final conjoined-balanced condition is now running serially; preserve its frozen inputs and finish its audits before comparing conditions.
research/project/decision_log.md:141:Document the researcher's expectation that an initial reasoning breakthrough may take hours, while retained learning could make subsequent successes and related learning more efficient, using the first Rubik's Cube solution as an analogy. The proposed calculation compares fresh versus prior-memory acquisition experiences/time under matched controls; repeatability, causal persistent learning and transferable reasoning remain separate claims. Status: hypothesis and proposed diagram only, not a frozen experiment or an exponential-improvement result. No code, running experiment or gate changed. See [design and calculation](../../documentation/design/research-goals/learning-efficiency.md) and [journal](../journal/discussions/2026-10-06-learning-efficiency.md).
research/project/decision_log.md:182:2026-10-06 delta integration boundary: paired helper may compare shortlist and all-legal choices only under one frozen memory snapshot. Require omission reporting and matched timing before any latency claim; helper fixture passes, full graph pending.
research/project/decision_log.md:190:2026-10-06 focused interface gate: audited adaptive memory retains KQK correction when 24/8 delta shortlist is used; both fixtures focused choices independently succeed and match all-legal. Treat as familiar persistence/interface evidence only; next gate is disjoint/counterfactual consequence-sensitive transfer.
research/project/decision_log.md:192:2026-10-06 counterfactual probe: reusing the audited adaptive memory on a support-removed KQK position changes the all-legal and focused choice from familiar `f7h7` to `f7a7`; both interfaces agree. The formerly reviewed `f7g7` is not repeated, but the chosen counterfactual move fails the one-ply forced-mate certificate and the position has no declared successful alternative. Record this as sensitivity/stale-pattern rejection only. Do not call it transfer or reasoning; the next transfer fixture must provide a verified positive alternative and remain disjoint from training.
research/project/decision_log.md:194:2026-10-06 delayed-sacrifice counterfactual: the positive-alternative diagnostic pair is now recorded. The same learned memory chooses failing `h5h6` on the original and successful `h5e8` after support moves; all-legal and focused interfaces agree. Preserve as an engineering probe only: it does not establish that the delayed sacrifice was learned, because the memory was trained on different fixtures and the original row fails. A future transfer gate must use disjoint families and predeclared positive alternatives.
research/project/decision_log.md:208:Use the four recommended papers to motivate separately pinned memory-preservation, timing/omission and shared-versus-local modulation diagnostics. Existing two-valence channels and per-edge memory already satisfy part of the structural advice; changing kinetics requires cell-type-specific evidence and fresh gates. Do not replace the intended learner with Jiang's gradient-optimized recurrent circuitry or distributional DQN. Preserve active smothered acquisition and older recovery intervention failures. Six saved development receipts reproduce exactly; no graph inference or successful repair is claimed. See [reading notes](../literature/fushiki-reading-notes-2026-10-07.md) and [journal](../journal/experiments/2026-10-07-fushiki-literature-review.md).
research/project/decision_log.md:210:2026-10-07 smothered prefix: distinguish initial omission from correction reversal. c4b4 is directly reviewed and initially suppressed, then returns above alternatives during distinct reviews. Diagnose memory recovery/representation/transmission only after frozen control completion; do not retune active protocol from prefix evidence.
research/project/decision_log.md:216:2026-10-07 fixed-schedule inference boundary: current absent/shuffled/disabled controls replay adaptive experiences, not fixed experiences. Any fixed-schedule success is an exposure diagnostic, not a causally controlled fixed-acquisition result. A future fixed positive-exposure test requires its own matched experience controls. Eight adaptive receipts now independently pass complete certificate binding, memory continuity and exact recurrence checks in adaptive-phase-audit.json.
research/project/decision_log.md:218:2026-10-07 positive replay diagnosis: first c4g8/PAM02 event has0active eligible KCs and0changed edges across84PAM02-associated edges;39changes are PPL103-associated. Investigate candidate-specific eligible positive projection after completing frozen experiment. Delivered reward alone is insufficient; do not conflate all changed edges with positive memory formation.
research/project/decision_log.md:230:2026-10-07 positive eligibility probe: after terminal acquisition audit, run one independently checked PAM02 replay from fresh memory under each of the four pinned input variants. Original projection has0 active positive-associated KC entries and0 changed positive-associated edges; balanced has10 entries/10 changed edges; combined has12/12. This diagnoses input eligibility for one replay only. It does not establish acquired choice, controls, transfer or reasoning; preserve the acquisition failure. See [probe report and audit](../../archive/early-development/research/reports/smothered-positive-eligibility-v1-2026-10-07/README.md).
research/project/decision_log.md:232:2026-10-07 matched forcing-prior ablation: on the same inspected three-ply smothered position, seed, forcing candidate set, and four-evaluation/four-simulation budget, neural-only priors selected a verified failure (`c4b4`), while mixing a fixed forcing prior selected the verified success (`c4g8`). Neural-only root priors were nearly uniform. Neither search reached a terminal leaf, delivered feedback, or changed persistent memory; the structural tag is an engineered search bias, not learned reasoning. Keep it opt-in and require multi-position/counterfactual matched evaluation plus a learning condition before broader claims. The next learning bottleneck is converting verified selected-choice and alternative consequences into useful persistent neural rankings. See [matched report](../../archive/early-development/research/reports/matched-forcing-prior-ablation-2026-10-07/README.md).
research/project/decision_log.md:236:2026-10-07 contrastive learning screen: froze original/balanced cues with informative, absent, shuffled and disabled controls. Independent audit passed all 54 certificate checks, 10 search-trace replays, 12 recurrence checks and matched exposure checks. Neither informative condition repaired the all-legal or fixed-search choice; all controls also remained failures. Balanced moved the known success from rank24 to rank6 but still chose a failure; original moved it from rank14 to rank17. Do not claim useful learning or input superiority. The phase ledger showed candidate presentation dominates search wall time. A same-position matched teacher-search rerun changed only forcing-prior mix from0 to0.5: presentations49->26, search16.76->8.00s, checked failure c4b4->checked success c4g8. This is an engineered search improvement, not learned reasoning. Next test whether feeding such better-selected verified consequences improves the fly's own ranking against matched controls. [Screen](../../archive/early-development/research/reports/contrastive-feedback-screen-v1-2026-10-07/README.md) · [forcing-prior rerun](../../archive/early-development/research/reports/forcing-loop-v4-2026-10-07/README.md).
