research/project/decision_log.md:399:2026-10-07 TERMINAL capture-retention transfer v3: completed the frozen 5-seed x 4-condition assay and independent per-run audits. Informative=5/8 final correct in every seed, identical to each control; te-01/te-05 counterfactual fails in every seed. Informative mean margin +0.0014369, but paired mean margin differences are -0.0006754 vs no-channel, -0.0017092 vs shuffled, and -0.0006544 vs disabled. Registered transfer gates fail. The seed-independence audit finds one effective functional replica: direct stimulation with zero model input bypasses seed-randomized input weights, and MBON readout bypasses the randomized head. Treat seed-bootstrap uncertainty as conditional on this deterministic model, not evidence across independent initializations. Do not interpret memory changes as learning success. Full evidence: research/reports/capture-retention-assay-v3-2026-10-07/README.md.
