research/project/decision_log.md:474:2026-10-08 interpretation correction/pivot: final common-memory probes show informative taught-context contrast +43.56%, exceeds no-channel/shuffled/disabled. Earlier wording that learning was unsuccessful was too broad; choice repair/transfer remain unmet but persistent contrast adaptation occurs. Cross-event scores were incomparable for final contrast. Keep diagnostic post-hoc, no promotion/new gates; next distinguish criterion readout from action preference rather than replace encoder solely from overlap. See ../reports/delayed-common-memory-diagnostic-2026-10-08/README.md.
research/project/decision_log.md:534:Historical receipts show the gamma2 candidate receives almost identical baseline Qe6/Qh7 eligibility (cosine 0.9999999658), while the existing conjoined encoding directly stimulates none of its KCs for either move. A static all-legal check finds seven of 26 moves with zero candidate coverage. Reusing the unchanged conjoined encoder with the declared 120-KC gamma2 pool, unchanged seed and dose, removes these coverage gaps without identical full cues; overlap increases. This is an engineered input hypothesis, not neural learning evidence. Next compare rule and pool factors separately on the same anatomical mask. No graph dynamics, training or source-rule change occurred. See [raw evidence and mistake record](../../archive/early-development/research/reports/plasticity-timing-candidate-2026-10-09/README.md).
research/project/decision_log.md:554:## 2026-10-09: Bind rate timing to recorded frames and memory checkpoints
research/project/decision_log.md:556:Previous goal turn was progress: graph-path evidence and rate integration changed the available next action. Added RateTimingMemory as an unintegrated gamma2 branch consuming all recorded recurrent intervals, using an explicit fixed-model reference and numerical step duration. Separate gains, KC credit and short/long local response states persist across consumed frames and enter snapshots. Existing base/sign validation and magnitude updates are reused; the old endpoint API is refused. Disabled handling holds all memory states fixed. Inert four-cell arrays verify continuation, scoped mapped changes, validation before mutation and reference-bound identity. No SparseTrainer or graph dynamics ran in these new checks.
research/project/decision_log.md:558:This adapter holds gains during each precomputed neural frame and applies them afterward. That approximation and the above-reference normalization are explicit engineering choices; neither establishes a natural reward pathway, biological clock, online retention or transferable chess behavior. The actual annotation-authenticated mapping, schedule, model reference and coordinator adapter remain unfinished. No training was run. [Specification](../../documentation/design/neural-learning/rate-timing-memory.md).
research/project/decision_log.md:560:Mistakes and fixes: inspection guessed a nonexistent stockfish-value-lesson-brain filename; file discovery showed no matching module, so no claim relies on it. Review identified that a valid finite gain could still overflow its Float32 effective magnitude during restore; added representability validation before mutation. Historical files and failed candidates remain preserved. Raw full-suite verification: research/reports/plasticity-timing-candidate-2026-10-09/npm-test-rate-memory.txt.
research/project/decision_log.md:580:Gate-relevant question: does restricting the existing conjoined encoder to the authenticated gamma2 KC pool produce distinguishable actual local neural rate trajectories on the 26 legal moves of the historical development board? Compare the existing versus restricted pool with the same seed, dose and untouched model parameters. Measure full KC/DAN trajectories and fixed MBON readouts; no plasticity module, feedback pulses or parameter setter will be called. Hash all parameters/anatomy before and after, stream receipts, checkpoint bounded progress, use heap 256 MiB/duty 0.5/RSS 768 MiB/free-memory 256 MiB guards. One serial graph diagnostic is planned.
research/project/decision_log.md:592:Added a bounded temporal feedback planner using the existing independent consequence verifier. It binds board/history, task, move, actor, status and proof digest before encoding; unknown produces no frames. Cue timing stays fixed while verified success/failure select an explicitly engineered early/coincident PPL103 pulse. Informative, absent, disabled, fully swapped and scheduled-shuffled conditions expose their exact frame/pulse semantics. No teacher parameter delta enters the plan.
research/project/decision_log.md:600:TemporalFeedbackSession binds all-legal pre-feedback assessment to independently checked evidence, retains neural continuity during frames and local memory traces across lessons, and checkpoints the next unacknowledged frame. Inert mechanical fixtures verify prefix resume, completed-frame finish without replay, failed-frame rollback, disabled memory isolation, stale assessment and malformed checkpoints. All 214 software tests pass; these fixtures do not establish neural learning.
research/project/decision_log.md:610:Exact command: node --max-old-space-size=256 research/reports/plasticity-timing-candidate-2026-10-09/run-temporal-hypothesis.mjs --protocol research/data/gamma2-temporal-hypothesis-v1/protocol.json --cpu-duty 0.5 --out runs/gamma2-temporal-hypothesis-v1. Process exited 1 during first all-legal assessment: readMBON requires population arrays but caller supplied precomputed means. One candidate evaluation followed reference evaluation; no lesson start, feedback event or memory update occurred. Checkpoint-1 and source snapshots remain preserved in the failed run directory. This is a runner interface failure, not evidence against the plasticity hypothesis. Correct the shared readout call to supply arrays, preserve v1 protocol/pins, register v2 with identical scientific parameters and gates, and launch into a new directory. No ongoing process or timeout is being mistaken for failure.
research/project/decision_log.md:618:Independent auditor construction found that v2 stores raw local rates and memory identity but omits explicit fixed-reference arrays. This prevents rate normalization replay from receipts alone; it does not prove neural feedback failure. Active pinned code/protocol is untouched. Correction for this run: once training is terminal, the auditor reconstructs the exact pinned from-scratch model and one unstimulated forward reference, authenticates the resulting memory identity against every arm, then replays local numerical updates from saved rates. This is a separate read-only reference reconstruction, not another training run or selected checkpoint. It uses the same sparse heap/RSS/free-memory/duty guards. Numerical audit shares the declared integrator and cannot constitute independent biological validation. Future protocol should record local reference arrays directly; no next protocol is created while the run is active.
research/project/decision_log.md:622:The serial hypothesis-only training process completed (exit 0): 152 feedback frames, 189.453125 MiB peak RSS, 330.4097108 s elapsed, CPU user170.437 s/system5.469 s, heap256/duty0.5. Separate read-only auditor completed (exit 0), reconstructing the omitted pinned reference and replaying all 152 recorded local updates. Topology, signs and all nonplastic parameter hashes match before/after every arm; disabled memory is identical throughout. Receipt/certificate/plan checks pass. Audit numeric replay shares the integrator and ranking arithmetic uses saved readout arrays; it is not independent biological or complete graph-response validation.
research/project/decision_log.md:632:The prior protocol was not adaptive, despite adaptive targeting being a stated design weakness. This is a design mistake now recorded. New [gamma2 adaptive current-error protocol v1](../../archive/early-development/research/data/gamma2-adaptive-target-v1/protocol.json) selects the unique unaided all-legal top choice only after checking its independent certificate says failure; otherwise the run aborts. It pairs that actual selected error with the already certified Qh7 solution. Informative, fully swapped, absent and disabled arms each measure their own initial choice, have the same two-action/152-frame dose, and replay proofs. Gates are frozen: target-edge direction and pair-margin specificity, exact disabled-memory isolation, and whether Qh7 becomes the unique all-legal top move. There is one seed and one acquisition pass; a pass does not establish reliable chess learning, retention, reversal, transfer or biology. Protocol pins runner and auditor separately, inherits v2 timing/memory/encoder/model, and preserves v2 outputs. No training has yet started.
research/project/decision_log.md:638:Protocol-v1 runner selected each arm's unique top all-legal move after independent certification. It was Qg8, a verified mate-deadline failure, followed by the certified Qh7 solution. The four conditions received equal cue/action schedules and 152 teaching frames. Separate auditor verified source pins, proofs, plan, complete pre-feedback rankings, 152 frame updates, topology/sign/fixed-state hashes and unchanged disabled memory.
research/project/decision_log.md:642:Diagnosis update: v2 correctly changed a focused Qh7/Qe6 margin but reviewed stale Qe6 while Qg8 led. V3 corrected the target and had a larger causal movement against the actual leader. Because the leader still won, stale targeting is a contributor but not the only blocker. The tested local association is stored selectively; its fixed MBON score effect remains too small relative to the observed all-legal gap. The current readout is an engineered preference, not a calibrated chess value or validated action circuit. Do not use a fitted coefficient, outcome-selected decoder or extra repeats on this same puzzle to declare a fix.
research/project/decision_log.md:650:Rechecked the primary MBON output study while interpreting the two failed all-legal puzzle runs. Aso et al. 2014 supports a distributed MBON ensemble representation of learned valence that biases memory-based action selection. Their result does not establish MBONs as one-neuron motor commands, nor does it validate the project's fixed `mean(MBON12)-mean(MBON01)` score as a 26-action chess value. The 2021 downstream connectome study maps multiple convergence neurons integrating MBON learned value and lateral-horn innate input, further underscoring that an output interface must be declared and tested rather than inferred from one score.
research/project/decision_log.md:652:Primary-source search snippets were inspectable; direct eLife/PMC pages returned bot challenges in this session, consistent with prior documented retrieval limits. No newly retrieved full text or exact quantitative claim is used. These are already registered research lines, used here only for the bounded claim that MBONs bias actions and the specific subtraction remains engineered. Sources: Aso et al. 2014, https://elifesciences.org/articles/04580; Eschbach et al. 2021, https://elifesciences.org/articles/62567.
research/project/decision_log.md:654:Interpretation: local temporal association is now causally distinguishable from shuffled feedback and changes the candidate margin, but it fails the chess action gate even when feedback targets the model's current top error and the direct cues have zero overlap. The unresolved object is the entire cue-to-choice path: cue transfer into the mapped KCs, scope of eligible synapses, propagation through the fixed graph, and the engineered decision comparator. Do not fit the comparator on the existing puzzle/result. Any next graph run must pre-register one bounded target readout/input hypothesis, include informative feedback alongside the matched controls, and test the learner's fixed all-legal choices on held-out puzzle families. The frozen v4 assay's biological identity/reversal blockers still apply to that assay.
