research/project/decision_log.md:860:Resume3 disappeared after publishing checkpoint008028 during disabled-plasticity interference. No stderr captured, so the exit cause is unknown; free system memory was about380MiB near exit and recovered after, compatible with but not proof of the 256MiB free-memory guard. A first recovery attempt failed before graph load because the runner requires a nonexistent output directory; the empty failed output/log artifacts are preserved as resumed4. Resume5 branches from the completed checkpoint008028 under unchanged pins, with stdout/stderr captured outside the runner-owned output directory. PID15964 was live at checkpoint008034. This is continuation of matched exposure, not an extra run or gate advancement.
research/project/decision_log.md:880:Extended the exploratory G0 schedule analysis to compare acquisition-plus-reversal target-cue label history against reversal truth, since arm memory persists across those phases. The frozen schedule aligns36/64 assignments; the 512-seed sample mean is31.98828125, with117/512 at least as aligned. Frozen source hashes and schedule hash reproduce. This is assignment history only and does not explain the neural margin/accuracy result. No G0 gate or frozen protocol changed. [Report](../../archive/early-development/research/reports/curriculum-g0-shuffle-control-diagnostic-2026-10-12/README.md).
research/project/decision_log.md:886:Diagnosed the silent G0 audit as slow but active: it replays all6,736 receipts and neural recurrence under0.5 duty pacing; PID8180 advanced CPU time, read about91MiB and remained within memory limits. The auditor previously wrote only at completion. Preserved the exact launched source by SHA-256 and added periodic progress JSON every500 receipts to the auditor for future runs. Syntax check passed. The active replay continues unchanged; no restart, duplicate audit or learner/protocol change. G0 remains failed pending audit completion. [Journal](../journal/experiments/2026-10-11-curriculum-g0-receiver.md).
research/project/decision_log.md:928:2026-10-19 10:33 Asia/Jakarta: Preserve both frozen G0-history auditor failures: retry1 terminated at 4,500/14,161 receipts and retry2 at 4,000/14,161 on the same RSS/free-memory assertion; neither published an audit. Process observations place RSS near170MiB while free RAM fluctuated, making the free-memory clause the likely but not recorded exact cause. Keep all original sources and failed logs. Register a separate audit copy that waits below the existing256MiB floor and retains all replay, CPU and RSS limits. Its source/protocol hashes and exact scope are recorded in [the audit package](../../archive/early-development/research/data/g0-reversal-history-audit-wait-v1/README.md) and [dated journal](../journal/experiments/2026-10-19-g0-audit-memory-guard.md). This is read-only evidence recovery; no diagnostic training, gate or scientific outcome changed.
research/project/decision_log.md:1007:Next larger hypothesis, before implementation: vectorize independent neuron rows into separate SIMD lanes while retaining original per-row f64 multiplication/addition order. This differs from reordering/reducing edges inside a row. Pair/pack rows by degree with explicit original-neuron mapping, mask padding rather than changing zero-sign arithmetic, and gather previous-state values. Original sparse topology/indices remain available for local learning and gradients. No implementation or expected speedup; potential gather/padding/layout/update memory costs might defeat it. Register primary SIMD opcode/semantics and layout sources before experimental use, estimate bounded allocations, then test exact histories/updates and actual pipeline performance in a separate version. Existing frozen reuse trial is untouched. This is our engineering derivation, not a literature-backed local performance claim.
research/project/decision_log.md:1039:Next structural persistence hypothesis is the previously recorded bounded-replay checkpoint design: instead of publishing134209 transient values twice per frame, persist lesson-start local memory, verified immutable stimulus plan/prefix, exact cursor/current memory/pending receipt and a versioned binary state digest. Reconstruct at most32 frames on resume through the original neural/plasticity path, reverify certificates, compare final memory/chain/state hash and never acknowledge or double-apply a mismatched update. Full from-scratch graph still runs during teaching; only deterministic transient storage is derived. Recovery cost must be counted and bounded. Binary evidence/typed snapshots are an explicit new schema/identity with independent numeric comparison to legacy states; never silently substitute historical hash identities or omit durable barriers. This is unimplemented and requires a separate protocol, recovery faults and full pipeline proof before use. It directly targets measured serialization/snapshot/hash work and is prioritized before unmeasured SIMD layout work if the new classifier improves actual speed.
research/project/decision_log.md:1044:Proceed with a separate engineering candidate under documentation/design/evaluation-and-performance/derived-episode-checkpoints.md: typed rollback, versioned binary state hashes, lesson-start physiological memory and bounded verified replay before pending acknowledgement. Motivation is repeated serialization/hashing of a deterministic transient vector. No adoption or performance result; preserve all legacy formats and current compiled-row trial. Tests and full-graph work wait for the live trial/audit to finish.
