research/project/decision_log.md:1425:2026-10-24 - Fix goal (executed by Claude Code from 12:40; the 13:00 entry above names Codex, but this ledger's entries are Claude Code's) - task 1 pivot after reviewer finding 2: the retention probe is now reported with and without the Stockfish phase (v2, `outcome-only` condition, matched to v1), and the Stockfish child-position cue moves onto the move's own token family from the mover's side (`public-action-relative-cue-v2` + `CoupledStockfishBrainV3`, registration revision 7; new files, no pinned file edited) and is probed separately (v3). Reason: the v1 state cue shared about 2.6 of 15 cells with the move cue, so value pulses barely taught move choice yet caused ReversalMemory recovery. Interim probe v1 (eta 0.5/0.2/0.1): 0/4 retained at each; a no-graph cue analysis shows 21-27 of A's ~29 cue cells are also driven by the 10 interfering lessons, so cross-board cue overlap, not only inactive-cell recovery, is a measured candidate cause. Eta choice waits for all three probes. [Journal](../journal/experiments/2026-10-24-stage1-memory-retention-fix.md); [ledger](../../documentation/handoffs/fix-goal-ledger-2026-10-24.md).
research/project/decision_log.md:1427:2026-10-24 18:55 - Fix goal task 1 recorded as failed; memory path stopped (prompt task 1c). Three registered retention probes on training boards (with Stockfish, without the Stockfish phase, with the mover-value cue of registration r7) found no eta in {0.5, 0.2, 0.1, 0.05, 0.02} that keeps a taught board correct after 10 other lessons in 3 of 4 probes (best 1/4). The only allowed alternative, a slower dopamine-only recovery rule, lacks primary support for immediate memory in the modeled compartments (Aso and Rubin 2016: unpaired DAN activation reduced immediate memory in 4 of 5 DAN sets; resistance only in alpha1 or after spaced-training consolidation; Berry et al. 2012: DAN activity drives forgetting), and the probe evidence points to cross-board cue overlap that such a rule would not remove; it was not implemented (register entry 2026-10-24). Decision requested from the researcher (handoff): input-representation change before memory acceptance, a consolidation mechanism, the G0 RateTimingMemory receiver, or stopping Stage 1 with this receiver; and, separately, the Stockfish teaching target for D9 (absolute value saturated on these boards). Task 2 proceeds meanwhile. [Report](../../archive/early-development/research/reports/stage1-retention-probe-2026-10-24/README.md); [ledger](../../documentation/handoffs/fix-goal-ledger-2026-10-24.md).
research/project/decision_log.md:1431:2026-10-25 - Researcher decisions on the fix-goal task 1 stop (chat, 2026-10-25): (1) memory path = option (a): an input-representation change (task-3 class: public occupancy/candidate inputs, starting with the existing relational v1-v3 and bound-ray encoders) is allowed before task 1 acceptance and is judged by the same registered retention probe on training boards; not a consolidation mechanism, not RateTimingMemory, not a Stage 1 stop. Rationale: the measured candidate cause is cross-board cue-cell overlap (21-27 of ~29 cells), which no eta can separate. (2) Stockfish teaching target for D9 = a relative target (the move's value against the same board's alternatives) as a new versioned teaching condition with a new registration; not less decisive positions, not search-only. (3) Board f3-blocked-p0a: no special handling; recorded as unacquired and re-examined after the input change. [Ledger](../../documentation/handoffs/fix-goal-ledger-2026-10-24.md) L023.
research/project/decision_log.md:1433:2026-10-25 - After the build weakness audit the researcher delegated the memory fix ("you decide exactly what to do"). Decision 1: abandon the Gkanias charging-to-LTM branch before any run, because the pinned >=5-synapse graph gives MBON-alpha'1 no KC inputs. Decision 2: add the alpha1 reward long-term store (PAM-alpha1 -> MBON-alpha1, depression without DAN-alone recovery; Aso and Rubin 2016, Ichinose et al. 2015) beside the unchanged restrained ReversalMemory, as registration r10 with matched controls; PAM-alpha1 follows only verified task-success pulses. Decision 3: judge it with retention probe v5 (same rule as task 1b), with a predeclared spaced probe v6 as the only fallback. [Journal](../journal/experiments/2026-10-24-stage1-memory-retention-fix.md); [register](../literature/source-solution-register.md).
research/project/decision_log.md:1435:2026-10-26 - Memory fix, after probes v5 (one lesson) and v6 (spaced, three lessons) on r10 chose no eta (retained at most 1/4). Decision (Claude, under the researcher's delegation of 2026-10-25): do not take the predeclared stop; add one further store, the aversive PPL1-alpha3 -> MBON-alpha3 long-term compartment (Aso and Rubin 2016; Wu et al. 2017), because in 6 of 6 failed v6 probes the board's final choice was a move its own lessons punished, and only the reward side had a long-term store. Registration r11 (cue v4 unchanged); judged by spaced probe v7, matched to v6. If v7 chooses no eta, the memory path stops and is reported, with no further mechanism. This departs from the 2026-10-25 stop rule; the researcher may veto. [Journal](../journal/experiments/2026-10-24-stage1-memory-retention-fix.md); [register](../literature/source-solution-register.md).
research/project/decision_log.md:1437:2026-10-27 - Researcher decisions after the memory diagnosis (report `research/reports/stage1-memory-literature-and-surrogate-2026-10-27/README.md`): (1) representation first: before further memory work or graph runs, test without the graph whether any allowed input code supports transfer to held-out training families, using a perfect-memory comparison learner; (2) Stage 1 encoder and memory work uses outcome-only teaching, because the absolute Stockfish target opposed the verified outcome on about 41% of probe v7 pulses; a relative Stockfish target returns later as its own registered condition for D9, which stays frozen, so Stage 1 cannot be accepted before that condition exists. Additional training families and restricted features (contact geometry, king-line collinearity) are not yet decided.
research/project/decision_log.md:1439:2026-10-27 - Researcher decision after step 1 (option A; report `research/reports/stage1-representation-ceiling-2026-10-27/README.md`): Stage 1 moves the Fly from the allowed occupancy cues (public-action-relative v1-v4, relational, bound-ray; at chance on held-out training families for a perfect-memory learner) to an attack-map input. For each candidate move, the input lists which enemy piece types can reach the landing square after the move (pseudo-legal; pins ignored), and marks each as standing on a clear line with its own king or not. This is an engineered perception feature in the restricted class (attack judgement; 2026-10-24 reviewer addendum). It does not model vision, and every claim must state that the Fly was given it. The Fly must still learn from verified outcome feedback which attacks matter, including that lined-up attackers often cannot recapture. Teaching for this work stays outcome-only (earlier 2026-10-27 decision). Additional training families remain undecided. Plan: a new versioned encoder, then a no-graph surrogate check of the r11 learner with it, then a registered graph probe.
research/project/decision_log.md:1467:- Expected cost: slower progress and possible early smoke failures. Benefit: a Stage 2 pass would support "learned mate from consequences, with engineered local input". Every claim keeps the engineered-input caveat.
research/project/decision_log.md:1479:- Review conclusion, not an experiment authorization: retain the distinction between engineered safe-capture learning, transferable reasoning in the model and reasoning in a living organism. The [external-review assessment](../../archive/early-development/research/reports/research-maturity-review-2026-10-30/README.md) records the evidence, 40 review themes and a prioritized confirmation path.
research/project/decision_log.md:1483:- Next decision: choose a bounded scientific claim and prospectively protected comparator/structural-family test before any new experiment registration. ISEF target is 2028 or later; eventual-year rules and student contribution remain separate checks. No experiment, teacher, memory, data or gate changed during this advisory review.
research/project/decision_log.md:1487:- Trigger: under cue v2 the Fly's response is a function of 28 engineered tokens (33 patterns in training), and a token lookup transfers 23/24 leave-one-family-out ([response report](../../archive/early-development/research/reports/maturity-review-response-2026-10-30/README.md)). Researcher: the existing evidence is biased and uncalibrated, and peer review would reject it.
