research/project/decision_log.md:1587:Both coupled and ablation main runs and separate audits complete: each6912 trials/48 trajectories,864 unknown. Coupled R=.602879 fails G3/G4; zero coupling R=.611021 fails G3. The phase-state diagnostic matches48/48 original coupled summaries. Slow A-negative/P remains near.9992 at T1; it has little old trace to protect. A further analytic residual is that coherent restoration at u=s=1 records no history. The next [metaplastic hypothesis](../reports/memory-retention-continuation-2026-10-31/metaplastic-proposal.md) directly addresses history at saturation. This is a different mechanism, openly counted as a new family under the researcher's removal of the bounded development end stop; it is not a coupling-rate sweep. Retention, acquisition and reversal must pass together. Source graph/training boundaries and original thresholds remain fixed.
research/project/decision_log.md:1593:The audited cascade still fails G3 and G4. Paired absolute A retention improves by.032285 while reversal margins regress by.078954/.090760/.118292. Do not select it. Primary-source review identifies a distinct four-state transition topology in Khorsand/Soltani2017 Figure6d, visually inspected: contradictory evidence first moves a protected state into a buffer, then can switch it directly into the opposite reservoir. [Fixed pre-data protocol](../reports/memory-retention-continuation-2026-10-31/reservoir-proposal.md), [analysis](../reports/memory-retention-continuation-2026-10-31/development-comparison-v1.json). Test this structural metaplastic revision with unchanged gates/inputs/exposure. No task-change detector, graph run or chess training is authorized or installed.
