research/project/decision_log.md:1705:Later addendum: the standalone audit v2 passes its full declared arithmetic/provenance scope under the unchanged 300-second guard after a bit-equivalent performance repair; preserve v1 timeout. Corrected activity counts reject weak/intermittent spillover as the sufficient description of the six strongly co-active KCg-d-to-MBON05 inputs. The source review plus absent retained KC-to-KC contacts do not support installing a lateral mAChR-B rule on those cells. Prioritize exact existing APL contact/arbor geometry and a source-supported representation condition; do not replace this with a global scalar or another ungrounded storage exponent. [Next discriminator](../reports/memory-interference-diagnosis-2026-11-01/next-mechanism-decision.md). Revisable storage, joint capacity/delay/interference performance and sealed confirmation remain required; the goal stays active.
research/project/decision_log.md:1708:The completed attachment analysis and separate brute-force sample arithmetic expose large branch sensitivity from small midpoint offsets. Preserve exact-geometry no-go, not a universal computational no-go. The researcher explicitly permits computational techniques to bypass this obstacle. Proceed with an approximate tree-kernel condition and geometry-sensitivity controls instead of waiting for complete endpoint acquisition. The two-pass kernel is a disconnected arithmetic prototype; inhibition normalization, feedback coupling and joint memory campaign remain to be registered before learner execution. [Prospective specification](../reports/apl-locality-feasibility-2026-11-01/computational-bypass-spec.md); [attachment evidence](../reports/apl-locality-feasibility-2026-11-01/attachment-result-and-next-gate.md). No claim of memory success or biological time.
